iling on desktop builds."]],0,530],[7161539,20409,35,1.341,1.058,[[8,21]],[["72232323_e9942dac",31,0,1,"`on the next browser startup`?"],["8e63ccc0_e4c34484",31,0,1,"`undoes`? `un-does`? Dunno, these all sound weird :)"]],0,531],[7162453,20410,4,0.157,0.113,[[7,65]],[],0,532],[7140600,20410,160,4.21,3.407,[[13,0.871,98,140],[20,0.129,45,20]],[],0,533],[7172504,20411,143,4.21,3.407,[[13,0.856,99,123],[20,0.144,46,20]],[],0,534],[7132100,20412,27,0.737,0.556,[[13,1.0,100,29]],[],0,535],[7184578,20413,15,0.037,0.015,[[11,23]],[],0,536],[7184778,20413,100,0.03,0.015,[[22,0.786,6,80],[11,0.204,23,20],[28,0.01,1,0]],[],0,536],[7184381,20413,2,0.012,0.007,[[29,0]],[],0,536],[7184658,20413,8,0.421,0.3,[[30,0]],[],0,536],[7184999,20413,8,0.421,0.3,[[0,75]],[],0,537],[7185523,20413,10,0.421,0.3,[[0,76]],[],0,538],[7185609,20413,4,0.015,0.004,[[29,0.5,0,2],[31,0.5,0,2]],[],0,539],[7185085,20413,4,0.015,0.004,[[29,0.5,0,2],[31,0.5,0,2]],[],0,539],[7201870,20417,5,0.259,0.185,[[13,101]],[],0,539],[7206528,20419,381,7.601,6.192,[[13,1.0,102,305]],[["5165f544_bc8a9797",32,0,1,"Also here: Move up to the fixture definition please"],["78c2fcb6_d23fc130",32,0,1,"Override `GetSetupSyncMode()` to be `NOTREACHED()` then, for clarity?"],["a3b2a7ae_81f9bff7",32,0,0,"Then no need to parameterize. Since the base SingleClientThemesSyncTest doesn't really do anything, I'd just inherit directly from SyncTest, and override GetSetupSyncMode() to always return…"],["c3d5529f_38ce567a",32,0,0,"As above, no need to parameterize then"],["f65245f2_4a927a48",32,0,1,"nit: Put the instantiation here, right after the class definition (that's the convention we're following, per the doc)"]],0,540],[7205132,20420,39,1.341,1.058,[[13,103]],[],0,541],[7209514,20423,472,6.547,5.298,[[32,0.714,18,340],[13,0.166,104,79],[7,0.056,66,25],[0,0.044,77,19],[17,0.021,5,9]],[["08b8ad6a_49d95b9a",33,0,1,"nit: I think this is worth a comment - custom settings with \"do nothing\" achieves that sync-setup-complete doesn't get set."],["7da0ba60_523b98af",34,0,0,"Should we also explicitly clear the history-sync bit? It'll *usually* be off by default anyway, but theoretically it could be explicitly enabled."],["a04eab49_cdb2a82b",6,0,0,"For my understanding: Do these changes mean that a bunch of browser tests were accidentally running in the sync-setup-incomplete state before?"],["af5d343e_432c9240",34,0,1,"nit: I think I'd just remove this TODO. If we're not merging it now, I'm pretty sure we're not gonna change it again later on. And TBH, I'm not even sure if merging would be better overall."],["b3bac36a_3ea989a8",35,0,0,"Is this recorded before or after the migration?"]],0,542],[7201166,20424,429,7.601,6.192,[[13,105]],[["329fb1f5_a59fb2be",26,-1,1,"nit: By convention, put the instantiation right after the class definition. Also for the other cases below."],["8bc7d5ec_a2f6bc3b",26,-1,0,"I'm assuming these tests were just moved, and not modified?"]],0,543],[7210926,20424,480,6.547,5.298,[[32,0.702,19,340],[13,0.163,106,79],[7,0.055,67,25],[0,0.043,78,19],[17,0.037,6,17]],[["408a15ab_fbba0380",9,-1,0,"Why did the CQ not catch that? Can you manually add a bot that'd cover this situation?"]],0,544],[7205001,20431,850,9.607,7.821,[[33,0.531,84,451],[13,0.458,107,392],[20,0.01,47,7]],[["3ad59721_e951dabf",36,-12,0,"Also `UserSelectableType::kOsPreferences`?"],["5c599788_edad4baf",37,-12,0,"I think this might become a problem on ChromeOS, where we might have to check `kOsPreferences` instead?"],["d0e0a590_bbc5a9d9",38,-12,1,"Okay, I *think* this is true, but it's not easy to follow... if the dual-layer store exists, then `user_prefs_` is always set to the account store, right? Not sure if this can be made clearer…"],["235b7a76_076899bc",39,-11,1,"`private:`"],["3ff21997_7faa2c35",39,-11,1,"This basically verifies that the bug (which this is fixing) exists, right? I think it might be worth pointing that out more explicitly, like with a reference to crbug.com/464008640. Generally, it's…"],["5b2581bb_636c4f68",39,-11,1,"`because the data types are not active yet` (right?)"],["5ee8d417_52922364",39,-11,1,"We don't really know it's stale, right? It could also be a legitimate remote update that happened while this client was offline, and we just don't know which of the two is more recent. This is…"],["725ec5b5_da0a1f33",36,-11,1,"`private:`"],["b67d3191_c2f0a3fa",39,-11,1,"Does this even matter in the `WithoutSelectedTypes` tests? If yes: All the tests set it - move into the fixture?"],["d00ef37d_4c01ed4f",39,-11,1,"`// Before sync starts up, the user changes a pref value. This gets written to the account store.`?"],["db32d5ce_5762fae1",36,-11,0,"optional: `EnableType` is kind of misnamed. I guess it's going to go away soon, but maybe we could rename it to something like `MarkTypeActive`?"],["0ba95e23_1d720988",26,0,1,"I'd add a note here that this test mostly documents the existing behavior, but it's not necessarily the \"correct\" or desired behavior."],["13a694c2_8e8568b4",26,0,1,"And here"],["31d144f2_1597c41f",26,0,1,"Similar here: This is the existing/old behavior, but not the \"correct\" one."],["387cb12a_67be59b2",38,0,1,"nit: `refers to` (guaranteed by the CHECK above now!)"],["c1731028_c270348b",9,0,1,"nit: Mention that all of this is behind a feature flag"]],0,545],[7245491,20433,867,9.607,7.821,[[33,0.541,85,468],[13,0.449,108,392],[20,0.01,48,7]],[],0,546],[7245355,20434,2,0.13,0.082,[[10,7]],[],0,547],[7255515,20437,867,9.607,7.821,[[33,0.541,86,468],[13,0.449,109,392],[20,0.01,49,7]],[],0,548]]}